invariant: INV-19
file: bench/stack.py
catches: test/lint-stack-walk.sh
reason: the walk adds no edge for a call through a volatile function
  pointer, as it did before. The stack wipes call their frames that way,
  so every peak above a wipe leaves the wipe's frame out. In a host
  object the walk then put ch_p256_key_from_pem's peak at 1,472 bytes,
  where the frames through p256_wide_wipe_below add up to 3,760, and the
  ROLE=server SUITE=aesgcm ch_read peak at 2,192 bytes, where the frames
  through sha512.c's wipe add up to 2,416.

--- old
            target = loaded.pop(fn)
            callees[target] = max(callees.get(target, 0), pushed)
--- new
            target = loaded.pop(fn)
